
ALGORITHM: Brute-Force Convex Hull

INPUT:
    A set P of n two-dimensional points

OUTPUT:
    The points forming the convex hull boundary

1. Set hull_edges = an empty list.

2. FOR every pair of distinct points A and B:
       Set left_side = FALSE.
       Set right_side = FALSE.
       Set collinear_points = an empty list.

       FOR every point C other than A and B:
           Calculate cross product:

           cross = (B.x - A.x) * (C.y - A.y)
                   - (B.y - A.y) * (C.x - A.x)

           IF cross > 0:
               Set left_side = TRUE.
           ELSE IF cross < 0:
               Set right_side = TRUE.
           ELSE:
               Add C to collinear_points.
           END IF
       END FOR

       IF points exist on both sides:
           Reject pair A, B as a hull edge.
       ELSE:
           Check whether any collinear point lies
           between A and B.
           If one does, reject this pair.
           Otherwise, accept A, B as a hull edge.
       END IF
   END FOR

3. Collect all endpoints of accepted hull edges.

4. Arrange the hull vertices in boundary order.

5. Display the hull vertices and boundary edges.

END ALGORITHM

